# Paths Semgrep should not scan, in .gitignore syntax.
#
# Semgrep already limits itself to files tracked by git, so node_modules,
# build/ and coverage/ are excluded by .gitignore without needing a line
# here. This file is for paths that ARE tracked and ARE meant to be, but
# are not application code.

# Reference material, not application code, and not served by the app.
#
# Note this is the repository-root examples/ tree, which is a DIFFERENT
# thing from public/examples/. public/examples IS served -- DMNTab.jsx
# fetches /examples/organizations/svb/... from it at runtime -- and must
# keep being scanned. The two trees have confusingly similar paths and
# only this one is inert.
#
# What it currently silences, all triaged in #112 and all in files the
# application never loads:
#   - duo/Handleiding Chat op de wet (uitgebreid).html
#       missing-integrity: no SRI on a cdn.tailwindcss.com script tag, in
#       a standalone documentation artifact.
#   - flevoland/.../BPMN/Python/archive/dashboard.py
#   - flevoland/.../BPMN/Python/archive/runner.py
#       flask render-template-string, in an archived demo of an unrelated
#       BPMN project. runner.py renders a module constant with no
#       interpolation at all.
#
# If anything under examples/ ever becomes application code, delete this
# rule rather than carving an exception into it.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing. A bare `examples/` is .gitignore
# syntax for "a directory named examples at ANY depth", which also
# swallows public/examples/ -- verified: it silently dropped
# public/examples/organizations/svb/RONL_BerekenLeeftijden_CPRMV.dmn,
# the file DMNTab.jsx fetches at runtime, from the scanned set. Anchoring
# to the repository root is what keeps the distinction above real.
/examples/
